WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.310
SCP-049 is a fascinating bundle of contradictions.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:10.700
Arguably, he’s the Hannibal Lecter of the
anomalous world: He’s educated, refined,

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.700
and cultured.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:17.560
A scientific man with scientific goals, capable
of communicating eloquently in both English

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.290
and Medieval French.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:24.940
As anomalies go, he’s one of the more cooperative
ones contained by the SCP Foundation, willing

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:30.890
to understand reason and even showing a small
degree of respect for his “fellow” researchers.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:37.260
And yet, despite all this intelligence and
refinement, underneath his dark, organic cloak,

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.930
a heart of deep red violence steadily beats.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:46.370
He’s capable of ending life with a mere
touch - causing all biological functions in

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:52.050
the body to simply cease through means that
are still unknown to science, thanks to a

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:57.949
series of inconclusive autopsies on SCP-049’s
unaltered victims.

00:00:57.949 --> 00:01:04.150
Not only is killing easy in a physical sense
for SCP-049, with a few notable exceptions,

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:07.860
it’s also been just as easy on his conscience.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:14.670
Such is the danger of the man or monster who
believes unshakably that his goals are righteous:

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:20.030
Any moral crime is permissible if done in
service of seeing them through.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:27.430
And for those who die at SCP-049’s hand,
an even greater indignity awaits: His inhuman

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:32.180
experiments, the gateway to a second life
as an abominable crime against nature.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:36.649
A glob of malignant spit in the eye of God.

00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:39.530
But let’s not get too ahead of ourselves
here, students.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:44.090
We’ve mentioned SCP-049 countless times
in passing before.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:49.659
Some of his strange tales, his interactions
with other anomalies like SCP-682, and even

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:54.890
with some of your questions and theories about
this bone-masked scientific madman.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:57.780
And yet, he still remains a mystery.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:03.020
Perhaps, to truly understand this fascinating
walking question, we need to return to the

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:08.550
beginning and give the classified files behind
the Plague Doctor a closer look.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:13.500
Like many of the most infamous anomalies discovered
by the SCP Foundation, the files indicate

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:18.360
that the discovery itself was first triggered
by a series of mysterious disappearances in

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:22.510
the sleepy town of Montauban, out in Southern
France.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:28.330
People across races, classes, ages, and genders
were simply falling off the map, suggesting

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:31.220
a highly indiscriminate assailant.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:36.310
Little did the Foundation know, in the beady
avian eyes of their killer, they all had an

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:43.080
extremely important commonality: Each and
every one of them was infected with The Pestilence.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:46.910
The Invisible Scourge, The Great Dying.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:52.050
Their killer was the only one with the proper
diagnostic mind to even notice the infection.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:57.130
He was the only one who could save the world
from this insidious, unseen threat.

00:02:57.130 --> 00:03:01.180
And then the SCP Foundation discovered his
laboratory.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:05.620
The Plague Doctor had been doing his delicate
work in an abandoned house on the edge of

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:06.620
town.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.800
The kind of place that gets whispered about
in local rumors.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.270
A bad place.

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:13.370
A cursed place.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:17.870
Little did they know, it was only the latest
in a long line of covert research centers

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:21.130
for this singularly inspired medicine man.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:25.010
While some of the details were a little foggy
in his memory, he’d been carrying out his

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:32.170
work for a little over 400 years now, moving
from place to place, causing strings of disappearances

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.050
wherever he showed up.

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:38.450
In his own words, he’s an extremely well-traveled
man.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:42.830
And still, the cure for that blasted Pestilence
continued to evade him.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:48.090
He sat in that decrepit Montauban house, surrounded
by groaning, writhing abominations of his

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:51.910
own creation, taking meticulous notes.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:57.150
Nothing would break his concentration, not
even the strangers in black tactical gear

00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:00.750
with large guns kicking in his front doors.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:05.450
His many Cured patients didn’t take kindly
to the intrusion on their treatment and decided

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:07.450
to swarm the interlopers.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:11.570
What followed was a violent struggle between
the Intruders and the Cured, resulting in

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:16.320
several of the Intruders injured and all of
the Cured dead once more.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:20.380
During all this chaos, the Plague Doctor never
once stopped taking notes.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:25.060
When he was finished with his sentence, he
willingly submitted to capture by this mysterious

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.380
“SCP Foundation.”

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:31.250
After all, when he told them about the true
nature of his mission, they would of course

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:34.750
see reason and allow him to continue his research.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:40.180
Sure, he may have committed a few crimes against
nature on the way, but he was working in service

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.350
of loftier ideals…

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:47.660
You can only imagine his profound relief when
he was first interviewed by SCP Foundation

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:51.340
Researcher Dr. Raymond Hamm in Site-85.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:55.500
He was in the presence of fellow scholars,
people of science!

00:04:55.500 --> 00:05:00.010
He worried at first that he’d been captured
by some group of common street scoundrels,

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:04.810
when in fact, the hands of providence had
delivered him into the perfect place to continue

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:06.220
his research.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:12.030
The warm light of fate was now smiling on
him after so long languishing in the dark.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:17.430
All he needed to do was allow the scientists
around him to conduct tests on his own body

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.380
while he conducted tests on others.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:24.970
At first, the SCP Foundation believed that
he was an anomalous human being wearing a

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:29.110
costume, but they soon discovered that he
was something very different.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:34.410
What they thought was a mask was actually
an outgrowth of his skull, a kind of insect-like

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:35.700
exoskeleton.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:40.310
The robes were also a component of his body,
a kind of thick hide that developed over the

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.310
years.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:45.590
The thickness of the hide itself also made
him impervious to a great deal of physical

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:46.990
damage.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:51.250
Despite his politeness, research notes on
the Plague Doctor indicated that Foundation

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.000
personnel found interacting with him “uncanny.”

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.889
There was an oddly eerie quality to him.

00:05:57.889 --> 00:06:01.560
Something indistinguishable that just felt
off.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:06.150
The Foundation also found that the Plague
Doctor, whom they initially addressed as “Doctor”

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:12.150
rather than SCP-049 out of a sense of mutual
respect, also came with a number of strange

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.950
personal effects.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:18.460
These included a long pointing stick, similar
to the ones used by medieval plague doctors

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.450
to touch things without fear of contamination.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.580
This stick was soon confiscated.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:27.990
It didn’t possess any anomalous qualities,
but the Plague Doctor had a tendency to gesture

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:33.180
grandly with it as he spoke, and the Foundation
feared he’d absentmindedly take someone’s

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.710
eye out with it if he wasn’t careful.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:39.980
The other two personal effects that the Plague
Doctor prized greatly was his old-fashioned

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:44.830
medical bag and the notebook that he obsessively
recorded his observations with.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:49.580
The medical bag, which seemed to exhibit anomalous
properties, contained a mix of archaic medical

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:53.830
tools as well as some that the Foundation
has been unable to identify.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:58.430
It’s through the tools in this bag that
the Plague Doctor is able to create instances

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:01.660
of SCP-049-2.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:06.240
As we alluded to earlier, the Plague Doctor
can kill with a touch, but that’s only part

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.280
of what he does to his victims.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:12.680
After causing all their biological functions
to cease, he takes the tools out of his medical

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:18.150
bag and begins performing crude surgery on
their corpse - Including using a syringe to

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:21.810
inject an unknown anomalous liquid into their
flesh.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:26.620
While the specifics of the Plague Doctor’s
modifications can vary from victim to victim,

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:32.330
the result is often the same: They’re converted
into strange, shambling abominations that

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.430
aren’t capable of any kind of higher thought.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:38.840
For the most part, their movements are extremely
basic and limited.

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:43.710
However, if they’re provoked, they can become
frighteningly violent, more than capable of

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:48.560
killing an armed Foundation guard if they
don’t remain alert during the engagement.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:54.639
The SCP Foundation was given a unique opportunity
to understand more about SCP-049’s twisted

00:07:54.639 --> 00:07:59.580
experiments: As part of his conditions for
containment, they agreed to provide the diabolical

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.550
doctor with a number of fresh test subjects.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:07.889
The Doctor was eager to continue his work,
and through watching him work, the SCP Foundation

00:08:07.889 --> 00:08:10.800
could learn a great deal more about him.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:15.550
Though we wouldn’t even pretend that the
Plague Doctor’s work has ever been enjoyable

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:16.660
to watch.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:21.470
They presented him with some live subjects
and a much greater number of mammalian corpses.

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:26.250
He would spend several days working intensely
on each one, then documenting his findings

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:28.030
in his precious notebook.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:32.610
As a mark of respect for the Foundation scientists
around him, the Plague Doctor was more than

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:36.460
eager to share his research with them and
compare notes.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:41.750
He was always a talkative one, perhaps just
excited to discuss his experiments and theories

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:46.180
with “like-minded” scholars after so many
years of working alone.

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:48.500
Here are four notable instances.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:52.630
First, the Plague Doctor was presented with
a live D-Class specimen.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:56.400
He thanked the Foundation greatly for this
gift, then set about his work.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:00.620
He asked the unaware D-Class several questions
about his medical history while retrieving

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:04.860
tools from his bag, before quickly touching
and killing the man.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:09.270
He performed extensive modifications on the
D-Class corpse, and when he was resurrected

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:15.740
as an SCP-049-2 instance, he was barely recognizable
as his original form.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:20.810
He was a bizarre, flailing creature, constantly
groaning and gasping from the oblong-shaped

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:24.390
hole that the Plague Doctor had carved into
his chest.

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:28.450
While performing this horrifying work, the
Plague Doctor eagerly remarked to the observing

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:32.230
researchers that the cure appears to be extremely
effective.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:37.800
Next, he was provided the corpse of a recently
deceased goat, which he also expressed gratitude

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:38.800
for.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:43.120
After performing surgery on the creature,
it was successfully resurrected into a bizarre

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.440
SCP-049-2 instance.

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:51.000
However, the Plague Doctor readily admitted
that this definitely wasn’t his best work,

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:54.960
commenting, “The disease was still in its
nascent stage.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:59.900
My veterinarian practice is rudimentary, but
the patient responded well to the procedure.”

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:03.899
Next, he was provided the corpse of a recently
deceased orangutan.

00:10:03.899 --> 00:10:08.530
The Plague Doctor was delighted by this - Commenting
that, given primate similarities to human

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:12.860
physiology, this would be the next best thing
from a true human test subject.

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:16.090
However, this research became surprisingly
fraught.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:21.310
He killed and reanimated the beast four different
times, seemingly unsatisfied with the result

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:27.160
each time, and when he failed to reanimate
the creature a fifth time, he seemed disconcerted.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:29.550
In a debriefing discussion, the Plague Doctor
said:

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:35.160
“I have learned so much from this, though
I fear my early optimism was misplaced.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:41.810
I hadn’t yet come across such a… a stumbling
block on my road to the cure.

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:45.310
More subjects like this would do a great deal
in advancing my research.”

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:49.380
Next, it was provided with the corpse of a
recently deceased cow.

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:55.650
This irritated SCP-049, who wanted test subjects
who were physiologically closer to humans.

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:59.050
Still, despite his frustration, he continued
his work.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:04.370
He only took brief breaks to enjoy a meal
of hard cheese, salted pork, and thin crackers.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:09.550
Tests showed that SCP-049 didn’t require
sustenance to survive, but he enjoyed the

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:13.010
act of eating and found that it helped him
with his work.

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:17.230
He embalmed the cow, rearranged its organs,
and even inverted its head.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.780
However, this didn’t impede his work.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:24.520
He injected it with a variety of liquids,
which he described as the essence of the humors.

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.660
When asked to elaborate further on this, he
said,

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:30.260
“The Pestilence may bring about a systemic
imbalance.

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:35.570
In such a case, before true healing can begin,
one must find the humors in balance or the

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.390
body will reject the cure.

00:11:37.390 --> 00:11:40.860
This is, of course, elementary knowledge for
the practical physician.

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:44.380
I would have thought you would have learned
this during your education!”

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:48.360
After being provided a working cattle prod
to introduce a little electricity into the

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:52.650
equation, the Plague Doctor successfully reanimated
the mutant cow.

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:55.540
From here, things started to go downhill.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:12:01.370
Dr. Hamm decided to conduct another interview
with SCP-049, hoping to get into the finer

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.890
details of his scientific process.

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:10.450
However, they hit some major roadblocks: SCP-049
seemed to be unable to actually articulate

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:15.280
the true nature of The Pestilence or his processes
in seeking the cure.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:20.589
Even his notebook wasn’t written in any
known language and proved impossible to decipher.

00:12:20.589 --> 00:12:25.000
As the interview went on, the Plague Doctor
seemed to become increasingly distressed,

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:29.380
insisting on the importance of his work to
helping the human race prosper and survive

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:31.050
this terrible plague.

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:34.130
All he needed in exchange was more test subjects.

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:38.560
The practiced civility that had been built
up between the Plague Doctor and the SCP Foundation

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:44.440
crumbled in 2017, after a tragic incident
in the Plague Doctor’s cell with Dr. Hamm.

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:48.200
When he entered to perform a very standard
interview with the Plague Doctor, the Doctor

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:52.310
appeared to become anxious and asked Dr. Hamm
if he was feeling well today.

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:57.070
Dr. Hamm thought nothing of it and tried to
continue the interview, but by that point,

00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:58.660
it was already too late.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:03.490
The Plague Doctor had come to believe that
Dr. Hamm was infected with The Pestilence.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:06.960
And of course, there was only one cure.

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:09.810
The Plague Doctor gave Dr. Hamm his touch
of death.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:13.930
The man died instantly, and the Plague Doctor
immediately went about turning his corpse

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:17.560
into another SCP-049-2 instance.

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:21.890
Because Hamm was killed so quickly, he didn’t
have time to activate his emergency security

00:13:21.890 --> 00:13:26.820
signal, meaning what was left of him wasn’t
discovered until three hours later.

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:31.310
Guards and researchers were horrified to see
one of their own turned into a mindless, deformed

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:35.230
monster by an anomaly they all thought they
could trust.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:39.510
Following this tragic incident, Dr. Theron
Sherman chastised the Plague Doctor for this

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:44.269
appalling breach of trust, and the cold-blooded
murder of Dr. Raymond Hamm.

00:13:44.269 --> 00:13:48.270
The Plague Doctor, in a state of increasing
distress, insisted that Hamm was infected,

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:51.149
and he did all he could to cure him.

00:13:51.149 --> 00:13:55.700
And while the Plague Doctor insisted a certain
level of scientific distance from his subject,

00:13:55.700 --> 00:14:00.360
it seemed that, deep down, he regretted the
loss of a friend and fellow researcher in

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.380
his endless quest against the Pestilence.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:08.089
After this incident, the Plague Doctor truly
became SCP-049.

00:14:08.089 --> 00:14:13.180
He lost all of his privileges and now remains
under lock and key in Site-19.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:18.010
Whenever he’s transported, he’s kept in
shackles and supervised by a number of armed

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:19.010
guards.

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:23.440
After discovering that the scent of lavender
has a pacifying effect on him, it’s regularly

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:27.290
used as a tranquilizer against him during
engagements.

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:33.490
This is how a cordial ally can become just
another prisoner in the eyes of the SCP Foundation.

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:38.959
In a summary interview after the Dr. Hamm
incident, Dr. Elijah Itkin asked if 049 had

00:14:38.959 --> 00:14:43.390
any regrets about the incident, noting that
he seemed oddly mournful.

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:46.709
049 paused, before replying,
“Mourn…

00:14:46.709 --> 00:14:47.709
Perhaps.

00:14:47.709 --> 00:14:49.370
I had not thought that…

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:55.080
It is lamentable that a fellow doctor became
infected, but the work continues.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:15:01.610
Regrettable as… as it was, Dr. Hamm's death
provided important insight.

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:05.930
Living human subjects are the only way to
proceed forward, I am decided.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:11.130
My cure is of little use on dead flesh, and
I have gleaned all I can from your generous

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:13.150
supply of corpses.

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:18.720
My desires turn towards tending to those still
living who suffer from the disease.”

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:23.140
Dr. Itkin replied that 049 would be disappointed
on that front.

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:30.700
He just laughed in response, and replied,
“Oh, Doctor, I wouldn’t be so sure…”

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:35.500
Now go check out “SCP-049 - What Actually
is the Pestilence?

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:40.490
The Plague Doctor Questions and Theories”
and “SCP-049 - Going Home” for more on

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:43.649
the enigmatic plague doctor, SCP-049!

